PART 4 — Blue → Violet proposal + WCAG AA proof (node dp-contrast.js, real math)
================================================================
MedSpark energy reference (HSL measured): stops sit S 75–95%, L 48–59%,
3-stop gradients at `to right`, glow shadows at 30% opacity.
PROPOSED (own hexes, same energy band):
  from #2563EB (h221 s83 l53) → via #5B54E8 (h243 s76 l62) → to #7C3AED
  (h262 s83 l58). Angle/stops/opacity mirror live (to-right, 3 stops, .3 glow).
White-text ratios: 5.17 / 5.41 / 5.70 — ALL PASS AA (>=4.5).
REJECTED: #8B5CF6 (4.23, FAILS — excluded from ramp).
For the record MedSpark's own orange CTAs (2.15/2.80/3.56) and emerald
Démarrer (2.54) do NOT pass AA with white — proposal is strictly compliant
where the reference is not. Surfaces/text: shell #0A0E17 kept (white 19.30,
matches structural dark-shell approach); text-secondary #9AA6C3 = 7.92 ✓.

